<section id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
  <h2 id="overview-heading">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Asimov</strong> is a Python package and interactive real-time vision system that can also be run as a standalone program. 
    It processes camera input via OpenCV, recognizes hand gestures using cvzone (which wraps MediaPipe), and provides configurable 
    visual effects and “glitches.” In <code>main_virtualcam.py</code>, cvzone is also used for face detection to implement a 
    “privacy eyes” overlay. Asimov includes utility functions for distance checks, logging, and safe path computation, 
    making it suitable for building interactive applications or demos. When run directly, it supports pluggable main loops 
    such as <code>main_virtualcam.py</code>, which showcase glitch effects and virtual camera output compatible with 
    OBS (tested) and Zoom (tested). meet.jit.si (Jitsi) does not currently work (black preview), and Discord sees the virtual camera in the 
    dropdown but shows a black frame. Legacy GTK-based demos exist but are no longer actively maintained.
  </p>
</section>
